 | `night_mode_toggled` (v2.54) | `action`, `mode` (str — CLOSED enum: `acceptEdits` / `manual` / `absent` / `other`; off-enum COERCED to `other`, never echoed — `bypassPermissions` is deliberately ABSENT from the enum so a tampered value can never be laundered into the signed chain as a legitimate posture), `previous_mode` (same closed enum), `result` (str — CLOSED enum: `applied` / `noop` / `refused` / `failed` / `other`), `hostname_hash` (str — EXACT 12-lowercase-hex sha256 prefix of the machine hostname, or exactly ""; bounded shape `([0-9a-f]{12})?`, RAW value validated — off-shape incl. oversize DROPPED to "", never truncated; the raw hostname is FORBIDDEN on the wire), `session_id`, `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-165 P2 / ADR-185 (2026-08-03) — records that the per-machine autonomy posture was toggled by `/night-mode`, emitted by `.claude/scripts/night-mode.py` on EVERY terminating path of `on`/`off` (applied/noop/refused/failed), never by `status` (read-only). Typed emitter `emit_night_mode_toggled`; dedicated deny-by-default `_NIGHT_MODE_TOGGLED_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch + closed-enum VALUE coercion, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: any filesystem path (settings overlay, marker), file contents, the raw hostname. NO ATLAS technique (operator-posture provenance, not a detection signal). |
 | `context_pressure_observed` (v2.56) | `action`, `used_bucket` (int — CLOSED set of PERCENT rungs: `40` / `60` / `80` / `90` / `95`; the unit lives in the field NAME. The check `_context_pressure_bucket_ok` is TYPE-strict: `bool` is rejected (it is an `int` subclass, so `True` would otherwise sail through any numeric test) and `float` is rejected even when it COMPARES equal to a rung (`40.0 in {40}` is `True` in Python), because `_lib/canonical_json.py` refuses floats in HMAC-covered fields and the spool writer then drops the ENTIRE event, leaving only an `audit-log.errors` breadcrumb — the same S181 / ADR-055-AMEND-2 class as `pair_rail_case.timeout_ms`. Anything off-set is COERCED to the sentinel `0`, deliberately OUTSIDE the enum so a consumer can always tell a real rung from a coerced one), `event_source` (str — CLOSED enum: `precompact` / `sessionstart_compact` / `userpromptsubmit` / `other`; off-enum COERCED to `other`, never echoed. Only `precompact` has a shipped producer in the PLAN-179 W0/W1 bundle; `sessionstart_compact` — the channel PLAN-179 debate amendment 8.1 designates PRIMARY — and `userpromptsubmit` are RESERVED, and a consumer MUST read their absence as “no producer yet”, NEVER as “no pressure observed on that channel”. The PostCompact `additionalContext` channel stays UNPROVEN until the PLAN-179 W0-1 probe lands and is therefore deliberately ABSENT from the enum), `plan_id` (str — strict `PLAN-NNN` shape via the shared `_compaction_plan_id_ok` validator, else `unknown`), `session_id` (present ONLY when the producer holds a session id derived from the HOOK INPUT; deliberately OMITTED otherwise rather than filled from `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID`, which an agent can set — an unattributed row is honest, a wrongly-attributed one is not; PLAN-179 amendment r1-C1), `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-179 W0 US2 / debate amendment 8.1 (ADR-153 continuity successor rail, 2026-08-18) — EDGE-TRIGGERED context-pressure breadcrumb: the session crossed INTO a new context-usage percent rung. A TRANSITION, never a per-turn sample — the hysteresis gate is `audit_emit.should_emit_context_pressure(used_bucket, state_dir)`, which persists the last rung in the marker `context-pressure-last-bucket` under the gitignored `.claude/state/` and FAILS OPEN (any state I/O error means “emit”: a bookkeeping file may never block or crash a user session, and fail-CLOSED here would silently lose the very signal PLAN-179 exists to measure). Without that gate the rail would append one row per prompt while the session sits in a single rung. Off-enum input never re-arms the marker — a bogus value must not be able to suppress the NEXT real transition. Emitted via `emit_generic` (no public typed wrapper — the `settings_tamper_detected` / compaction-pair precedent). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the raw token/byte counts, the exact percentage (a precise figure is a side channel on session size — the rung is the governance signal), the transcript text, the plan PATH text, the prompt body. NO ATLAS technique (governance/observability breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
